_np = [["Write a one-line promise for the campaign, such as 'ten new sign-ups from creators with under 20,000 followers in four weeks', and test every later decision against that sentence.", 'List three channels where your audience already spends time, then check each for ten minutes to see whether creators there post about products like yours.'], ['Turn each goal into a number and a date, for example 200 link clicks and 15 sales by day 30, so you can judge success without arguing about feelings afterwards.', 'Pick one main goal only; if you chase awareness, sales and sign-ups together, the brief becomes vague and no creator can tell what you actually want.'], ['Review at least twelve recent posts per creator and count how many comments are genuine sentences; a sudden jump in followers with few real replies is a warning sign of bought followers.', 'Ask each shortlisted creator for a screenshot of their audience ages and countries from the last 30 days and compare it with your target customer.'], ['Keep the brief to one page: goal, audience, three must-say points, two things to avoid, deadline, and how to label the post as sponsored.', 'Share one example of content you like and one you dislike, since creators understand a concrete sample faster than an abstract description of tone.'], ['Put the deliverables in writing with counts and dates, for example one video and two stories by 14 March, and state how many revisions are included before work starts.', 'Agree the payment schedule in advance, such as half on posting and half after seven days, and record who owns the content and for how long it may be reused.'], ['Give each creator a unique link or discount code so every click and sale can be matched to the right person, and test the link yourself before the first post goes live.', 'Check the live post within 24 hours for the sponsored label, the correct link and the agreed wording, and message the creator politely the same day if anything is off.'], ['Compare cost per result across creators by dividing what you paid by the sales or sign-ups each one produced, then rank them rather than relying on likes alone.', 'Wait at least seven days after posting before judging results, because many viewers act late, and record the final numbers in a simple table you can reuse.'], ['Build a one-page media kit with your best three posts, audience facts, and the types of partnership you accept, and keep the numbers updated every month.', 'Add a clear disclosure line to every sponsored post you make, and keep a log of each agreement so you can prove what was promised if a question arises.']]
